Fuad Tabba <fuad.tabba@linux.dev> writes:

> The kernel has no table for CP1256, the Windows code page for Arabic,
> so a vfat mount with iocharset=3Dcp1256 fails with "IO charset cp1256 not
> found".
>
> Add nls_cp1256 behind NLS_CODEPAGE_1256, with tables generated by a
> script from the Unicode Organization's CP1256 table. The only case pair
> outside ASCII is =C5=92 and =C5=93.
>
> Signed-off-by: Fuad Tabba <fuad.tabba@linux.dev>

Looks good too.

Thanks.

